being an excerpted few of the original 74 chapters from the full original, to the intent of condensing "the big picture" or "the continuous arc" of the full detailed sequence.

////
Editors notes:

Given the excellent introduction chapters provided by the author for Saul (ch0) and David (ch1), I sought whether something could be found for the transition to Solomon as well as perhaps an ending summary; in order to provide a bundle of chapters by which the full body of work might be usefully introduced to readers.

At this point I am  not carrying through with the idea; but leaving this artifact available should others see more clearly such a path, which I expect may benefit from some statements made by NCBS editors between chapters used.

////

